{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791625165,"nonce":"DmMBXshJvTOHmnuB1tH0EIqn0X4=","title":"Resolve var() for values read outside a rule","message":"A host that reads @keyframes blocks gets their declarations as written: Stylesheet::keyframe_declarations does not resolve var(), while rule declarations reach the host resolved. The resolution, Cascade::substitute, is private.\n\nAdd Cascade::resolve_vars(value, values): the value resolved as in a declaration of an element whose computed values are given (its custom properties, then the sheets' :root variables, then the theme's), so a keyframe can use theme tokens.","files":null}]}